{
  "$schema": "../../schema/vector.schema.json",
  "id": "sdk.transactions.atomic-beef",
  "name": "Atomic BEEF (BRC-95): the subject's graph, not the wire position",
  "brc": [
    "BRC-95",
    "BRC-62"
  ],
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "reference_impl": "bsv-rs@0.8.1: the expected values are this crate's ruling (BRC-95's graph followed through the inputs of every raw entry, proven or not; the owner's ruling of 2026-10-22), not the TypeScript SDK's. The bytes are the writers': @bsv/sdk@2.1.4, go-sdk@v1.7.2 and bsv-rs. @bsv/sdk 3.x (ts-stack 4d0ea63, Beef.ts:420-434) cuts the graph at each proven transaction and refuses the two vectors marked intended; it agrees on the other four",
  "parity_class": "required",
  "description": "An atomic BEEF is valid when the subject is a transaction of the BEEF and every other entry is reachable from the subject by following the inputs of raw entries, proven or not (this crate's ruling; @bsv/sdk 3.x stops at each proven transaction, as BRC-95's 'up to the point where each input can be confirmed with a Merkle proof' reads); position is not judged. Each proven entry carries a one-leaf BUMP (a block of one transaction, the root the txid); input.headers is the merkle root per height a chain tracker must carry. Every output is OP_TRUE and every unlocking script empty, so the spends execute. Staged in bsv-rs (tests/transaction/vectors/atomic-beef.json) for vectors/sdk/transactions/.",
  "vectors": [
    {
      "id": "dependency-order-subject-last",
      "description": "Dependency order, the subject last: Z (proven), C (unproven, spends Z), W (proven), S2 (spends C and W). As the Go writer writes it (a DFS over the inputs, the subject collected last; the order of the proven entries follows Go's map iteration).",
      "input": {
        "beef_hex": "",
        "headers": {
          "900000": "ad62ccc517cca1eed898ca62bc0a403d0792533ae87a5ce10a6aee883023eb5c",
          "900002": "9418fd90997d59d7855d73eb2f50ba6f3ef29305c472223540eff72bdbf1889f"
        },
        "writer": "go-sdk@v1.7.2 (2ca481c) Beef.AtomicBytes",
        "order": [
          "Z",
          "C",
          "W",
          "S2"
        ]
      },
      "expected": {
        "valid": true,
        "subject_txid": "5b9857114e6a0823e89d276a160502775633199adcffbbcfeadc72aa88265f2c"
      },
      "tags": [
        "brc-95",
        "atomic-beef",
        "happy-path"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ts-partition-order",
      "description": "The TypeScript writer's partition order on the same graph: every proven entry first in encounter order (W, Z), then the unproven in dependency order (C), the subject last (S2).",
      "input": {
        "beef_hex": "",
        "headers": {
          "900002": "9418fd90997d59d7855d73eb2f50ba6f3ef29305c472223540eff72bdbf1889f",
          "900000": "ad62ccc517cca1eed898ca62bc0a403d0792533ae87a5ce10a6aee883023eb5c"
        },
        "writer": "@bsv/sdk@2.1.4 Beef.sortTxs then Beef.toBinaryAtomic",
        "order": [
          "W",
          "Z",
          "C",
          "S2"
        ]
      },
      "expected": {
        "valid": true,
        "subject_txid": "5b9857114e6a0823e89d276a160502775633199adcffbbcfeadc72aa88265f2c"
      },
      "tags": [
        "brc-95",
        "atomic-beef",
        "happy-path"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "raw-unproven-ancestor-after-proven-descendant",
      "description": "The TypeScript writer's order on Z (proven) -> A (raw, unproven) -> P (proven) -> S1: P is written before its raw unproven ancestor A, which only P spends. BRC-95 judges the graph, not the position: valid. bsv-rs before 0.8.1 refused it UnrelatedTransaction (the bsv-dd x402 refund, P0-65). ts-stack 3.x (@bsv/sdk 3.0.0 at 4d0ea63, npm 3.2.1) refuses it: its closure (Beef.ts:420-434 #collectAtomicTransactions) does not follow the inputs of the proven P, so A is outside it and isAtomic is false (Transaction.fromAtomicBEEF: 'Atomic BEEF contains unrelated transaction data.'). The expected value is bsv-rs's ruling.",
      "parity_class": "intended",
      "skip_reason": "ts-stack 3.x cuts the subject's graph at each proven transaction and refuses a raw ancestor behind a proof; the expected value is bsv-rs's ruling (a stated divergence, bsv-rs CHANGELOG 0.8.1).",
      "input": {
        "beef_hex": "",
        "headers": {
          "900001": "15f26d2b3ed5ec37020d9022dc0e5308fe82b510af8477c9e7f80fd4bde430d4",
          "900000": "ad62ccc517cca1eed898ca62bc0a403d0792533ae87a5ce10a6aee883023eb5c"
        },
        "writer": "@bsv/sdk@2.1.4 Beef.sortTxs then Beef.toBinaryAtomic",
        "order": [
          "P",
          "Z",
          "A",
          "S1"
        ]
      },
      "expected": {
        "valid": true,
        "subject_txid": "3c383eeb0190db24cbff3b689cdf608d4d2e1bab6928f1fbe1eff0c7d5590285"
      },
      "tags": [
        "brc-95",
        "atomic-beef",
        "edge-case",
        "regression"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "subject-present-not-last",
      "description": "The subject present but not last: P, Z, S1, then A (S1's ancestor through the proven P, spending the earlier Z). Every entry is in the subject's graph and every unproven entry follows what it spends: valid. The TypeScript writer never writes this shape (toBinaryAtomic cuts every entry after the subject) nor does the Go writer (the subject last, the ancestry cut at each proof); bsv-rs's writer does, merged in the order P, Z, S1, A. ts-stack 3.x (@bsv/sdk 3.0.0 at 4d0ea63, npm 3.2.1) refuses it: its closure (Beef.ts:420-434 #collectAtomicTransactions) does not follow the inputs of the proven P, so A is outside it and isAtomic is false (Transaction.fromAtomicBEEF: 'Atomic BEEF contains unrelated transaction data.'). The expected value is bsv-rs's ruling.",
      "parity_class": "intended",
      "skip_reason": "ts-stack 3.x cuts the subject's graph at each proven transaction and refuses a raw ancestor behind a proof; the expected value is bsv-rs's ruling (a stated divergence, bsv-rs CHANGELOG 0.8.1).",
      "input": {
        "beef_hex": "",
        "headers": {
          "900001": "15f26d2b3ed5ec37020d9022dc0e5308fe82b510af8477c9e7f80fd4bde430d4",
          "900000": "ad62ccc517cca1eed898ca62bc0a403d0792533ae87a5ce10a6aee883023eb5c"
        },
        "writer": "bsv-rs@0.8.1 Beef::to_binary_atomic",
        "order": [
          "P",
          "Z",
          "S1",
          "A"
        ]
      },
      "expected": {
        "valid": true,
        "subject_txid": "3c383eeb0190db24cbff3b689cdf608d4d2e1bab6928f1fbe1eff0c7d5590285"
      },
      "tags": [
        "brc-95",
        "atomic-beef",
        "edge-case"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "unrelated-transaction",
      "description": "An entry outside the subject's graph: X (proven, spent by nothing) beside the S1 graph. BRC-95: nothing else may be present; refused. The TypeScript writer writes it (toBinaryAtomic does not trim an unrelated entry) and its 2.1.4 reader accepts it (Transaction.fromAtomicBEEF, Beef.verifyValid).",
      "input": {
        "beef_hex": "",
        "headers": {
          "900003": "8baacc2b54dfd5873298912d89061048e563e5a9b959c2a78c629b9b890e016c",
          "900001": "15f26d2b3ed5ec37020d9022dc0e5308fe82b510af8477c9e7f80fd4bde430d4",
          "900000": "ad62ccc517cca1eed898ca62bc0a403d0792533ae87a5ce10a6aee883023eb5c"
        },
        "writer": "@bsv/sdk@2.1.4 Beef.sortTxs then Beef.toBinaryAtomic",
